        "original_id": "e8abab31-39a9-5348-a77e-c578859161b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1976 German Grand Prix\n- People: James Hunt, Niki Lauda\n- Organizations: Lauda Air, Austrian Airlines\n- Topics: Formula One, racing helmets\n\nFacts:\n- The 1976 German Grand Prix was the tenth round of the 1976 Formula One season.\n- The 14-lap 1976 German Grand Prix was won by James Hunt.\n- Niki Lauda crashed at the 1976 German Grand Prix at the Nürburgring and barely escaped alive.\n- After retiring from racing in 1979, James Hunt became a media commentator and businessman.\n- Lauda Air was owned by Niki Lauda during much of its existence.\n- Lauda Air later became a charter airline subsidiary for the leisure operations of Austrian Airlines.",
